  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New module `camcraft_geometry::outline_text`. It reads a TrueType outline font and makes a typed string into closed shapes, in mm, on the layer `text`.\n  - `ttf.rs` is our own reader, written from the public OpenType specification. It reads `cmap` formats 4 and 12, `loca`, `glyf` (simple and composite glyphs), `hmtx`, `hhea`, `maxp`, `head` and the `OS/2` cap height. Each read has a bounds check.\n  - `mod.rs` flattens the quadratic contours to lines, with a chord error of 0.005 mm or less. It then makes a `SketchData` with closed chains only.\n  - `sample_font.rs` makes a small test font in memory. It has our own glyphs, so the repository stores no font file.\n- New undoable command `InsertOutlineText` (`crates/app/src/commands/insert_outline_text.rs`). It reads the font once at construction. The profile keeps the shapes, not the font, so the project file format does not change.\n- New MCP tool `insert_outline_text` (`crates/app/src/mcp/outline_text_tools.rs`). The tool is also in `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` (generated) and in the MCP guide table.\n- These inputs are refused by name:\n  - a font that cannot be read, a CFF font (`.otf` with PostScript outlines) or a font collection;\n  - an empty text, or a character that the font does not have;\n  - outlines that cross or touch;\n  - a height or a spacing outside the limits;\n  - a setup that does not exist, a setup with no stock, or a name that is in use.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3072-outline-text.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is a new feature (#3072). Before this PR, typed text was only single-stroke engraving text (`insert_text`, #2679).\n\n## Review fixes\n\n- Large curves keep the 0.005 mm chord tolerance. A curve can use up to 4096 pieces. A curve that needs more is refused.\n- Composite glyphs apply `SCALED_COMPONENT_OFFSET`. A component with both offset flags is refused.\n- Table reads use each declared table boundary. Character maps also use each declared subtable boundary.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-geometry --test outline_text`: 9 passed after the fixes.\n- Pin proof: the new tests remained in place while the original reviewed source replaced the fixes. All four new tests failed. The restored fixes passed all 9 tests.\n  - `large_curves_measure_inside_the_chord_tolerance`: at height 1000 mm, the old code exceeded 0.005 mm. The test measures curve-to-chord distance.\n  - `composite_offsets_use_the_component_transform`: the old code gave minimum `(1.0, 3.6)` mm. The test requires `(0.5, 1.8)` mm.\n  - `declared_table_lengths_bound_reads_with_trailing_bytes`: the old code accepted a declared `head` length of zero.\n  - `declared_cmap_subtable_lengths_bound_reads`: the old code accepted a short format 4 subtable. A separate mutation bypassed the format 12 length check and failed this test. Both restorations passed.\n\nFinal head: `46c7c9ecc33eb92808c572006775a8a8828addf5`. The quick gate ran against `upstream/main` `c484dd3d13b73259fff412e566db52f06e625a39`.\n\nThe shared `upstream/main` reference advanced to `ef157211438104997fc9e51f7e3affc4db303545` during the heavy release build. Heavy dry runs against both bases selected the same 242 steps, in the same order. The actual heavy run was initially planned against `c484dd3d13b73259fff412e566db52f06e625a39`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: **RED**. The run took 49.1 minutes. Of 1086 steps, 1081 passed and 5 failed.\n  - `blind_slot_pocket_family_cuts_from_end_wall_to_stock_edge` and `adaptive2d_spiral_and_offset2d_support_relief_while_trochoidal_and_do_not_touch_refuse` failed.\n  - `ui suites: lib` failed: 1418 passed, 8 failed and 7 ignored. One failure was `egui_app::post_dialog_tests::desktop_post_command_opens_dialog_and_applies_declared_script_options_undoably`; seven failures reported no graphics adapter.\n  - `ui suites: egui_app` failed three headless CLI tests. `ui suites: shell` failed one headless CLI test.\n  - The original PR body records the two non-UI failures and the desktop-post failure as pre-existing. This round did not run an independent baseline comparison.\n  - These failures limit verification. The full quick gate is red.\n- Clippy: **GREEN**, 111 seconds. Command: `cargo clippy -j4 -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-cl -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`.\n- The geometry outline suite passed all 9 tests. The app outline suite passed all 4 tests.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: **GREEN**, 34.2 minutes. All 242 reached app and motion steps passed. No step failed. Four known-fail probes failed as expected: three for #1950 and one for #2849.\n- The final head and worktree remained unchanged through verification. The latest upstream reference was still `ef157211438104997fc9e51f7e3affc4db303545` at completion.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- `app suites: example_catalog`: 37 passed and 4 ignored in quick, 12.64 seconds. The heavy gate passed all 4 ignored cases, 3.42 seconds. All 41 catalog tests ran.\n- `app suites: example_catalog_adaptive`: 1 passed.\n- `app suites: example_catalog_edge_work`: 1 passed.\n- `golden_cl`: 33 passed, 2.52 seconds.\n- No recorded program or golden changed. The final worktree is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `graphify update`: the command is not installed on this host.\n- UI screenshots: not applicable. This PR changes no UI code.\n\n- Toolpath generation on the text. A toolpath from the chains of any DXF-type profile is not on main yet: #1867 does that work. The test only pins that the pocket and the contour accept the text as closed chains.\n- A real third-party font file. The tests use the generated sample font only.\n- CFF (`.otf` PostScript) fonts. These are refused by name. A CFF reader can come later as a different issue.\n- The UI. This PR adds no dialog. The command is available through MCP.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2924 changes `crates/app/src/mcp/sketch_tools.rs` (`insert_text`). This PR does not touch that file.\n- #3304 changes `crates/app/src/commands/insert_text.rs`. This PR does not touch that file. It has its own name helper.\n- These PRs touch `crates/geometry/src/lib.rs`: #3061, #2999, #2993, #2992, #2981, #2979, #2978 and #2924. Each adds a line to the module list, so the lines are different. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Typed text in a TrueType outline font becomes a profile of closed shapes (letter holes included) for a pocket, V-carve or cut-out: MCP tool `insert_outline_text`, one undo step; unreadable or CFF fonts, missing glyphs and overlapping outlines are refused by name.\n\nFixes #3072\n",
